<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anxi Protectorate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">640–790</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Protectorate General to Pacify the West</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anxi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>, or Protectorate General to Pacify the West, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a>'s military government for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a> and the lands farther west. Founded in 640 at Jiaohe after the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaochang">Gaochang</a>, it moved to Kucha in 648 and oversaw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/four-garrisons-of-anxi">Four Garrisons of Anxi</a>. Weakened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a> and Tibetan attacks, it was lost to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetans">Tibetans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghurs</a> around 790.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anxi-protectorate.jpg" alt="Anxi Protectorate" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lệ Xuân · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tang_China_under_Emperor_Gaozong.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
